# Every variable RunOmics reads. Copy this file to .env.local and fill in what you use;
# .env.local is gitignored, so never commit real values.
# The coach commands (`npm run coach` and the other coach scripts) load .env.<profile>.local
# instead, with `dotenv -o`: that file alone, its values winning over the shell's.

# --- Garmin (the sync: scripts/sync.py, never on Vercel) ---
# The Personal API key, from https://connect.garmin.com/app/settings/personalApiToken.
GARMIN_PERSONAL_API_KEY=GCDC_your_personal_api_key
# Optional: a Garmin Connect token (from python scripts/get_secret.py) for what only Garmin Connect
# serves: shoes, the calendar, training status, race predictions, VO2max history, the coach's push.
# GARMIN_SECRET=eyJ...
# Optional, local only: the env file a refreshed GARMIN_SECRET is written back to - this file
# itself, e.g. .env.<profile>.local. Unset (as in GitHub Actions), a refresh lasts for the run.
# GARMIN_SECRET_WRITEBACK=
# Optional, only while GARMIN_SECRET still holds an old garth token: Garmin's OAuth1 consumer
# pair, for the day Garmin rotates the one scripts/garmin/auth.py ships with. Both or neither.
# GARMIN_OAUTH_CONSUMER_KEY=
# GARMIN_OAUTH_CONSUMER_SECRET=
# Optional: the Python the app's Garmin bridge and `coach:garmin-auth` start
# (default python3, or python on Windows, where python3 is a Store stub).
# RUNOMICS_PYTHON=python3
# The key's expiry date (YYYY-MM-DD) is a GitHub Environment *variable*,
# GARMIN_PERSONAL_API_KEY_EXPIRES, read by sync.yml only.

# --- Maps ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_TOKEN=your_maptiler_token_here

# --- Firebase client SDK (browser: sign-in, run notes, check-ins, push tokens) ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_firebase_api_key_here
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=your_firebase_app_id_here
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=your_firebase_sender_id_here
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=your_firebase_web_push_vapid_key_here
# The account `npm run set-owner-claim` grants the "owner" custom claim to.
# Provisioning input only: the UI and the Firestore rules both authorize on the
# claim itself, never on this email.
NEXT_PUBLIC_OWNER_EMAIL=owner@email.com

# --- Firebase Admin (server: push notifications, dedup state, the AI cache) ---
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=your-firebase-client-email
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY=your-firebase-private-key

# --- Language and time ---
# UI language, read at build time: en (default) or fr.
NEXT_PUBLIC_LOCALE=en
# Optional. The IANA time zone "today" is read in, e.g. Europe/Luxembourg.
# Pages are prerendered on a server (UTC on Vercel) and read in a browser;
# set this to the athlete's zone so both agree on the date. Unset, each uses
# its own local date. An unknown zone fails the build.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TIME_ZONE=Europe/Luxembourg

# --- Deployment ---
# Shared with the GitHub Actions workflows: authenticates their calls to /api/internal/*.
INTERNAL_NOTIFY_SECRET=a-random-secret-shared-with-the-github-actions-workflows
# Vercel Cron sends it as a bearer token to the scheduled routes in vercel.json; 16+ random characters.
CRON_SECRET=a-random-secret-for-vercel-cron
# Optional: this deployment's https:// origin, for the links pushes open. On Vercel it
# defaults to the production domain; without either, a push opens the home page.
# APP_URL=https://your-deployment.example.com
# Optional: true lets search engines index the site (the public demo); anything else is noindex.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOW_INDEXING=false
#
# The operator channel. A second athlete's deployment registers her devices, not
# yours, so its operator alerts (a failed workflow, a data token about to
# expire, the digest of phone errors, the coaching-block reminder) would reach
# her phone and never yours. Set both here and the deployment forwards them to
# yours instead, in English and titled with this deployment's
# GITHUB_SYNC_PROFILE. Your own deployment sets OPS_PUSH_SECRET alone: that is
# what opens /api/internal/ops-push to the other one. It is a shared secret of
# your own making - 32+ random characters, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32` - and
# the same value must be set on both deployments.
# OPS_PUSH_URL=https://your-own-deployment/api/internal/ops-push
# OPS_PUSH_SECRET=
#
# A private site - required for a real athlete's data, whose routes are stored
# as recorded, start and finish included. With RUNOMICS_PRIVATE=1 every page and
# API answers only to the owner (the "owner" claim) or an invited viewer;
# everyone else gets /sign-in, and an API a 401 (src/proxy.ts). Unset, the site
# is public: fit for the demo dataset only.
# Needs FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID above and SESSION_SECRET, which signs the session
# cookie: 32+ random characters, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`. Changing it
# signs everyone out. Private without a usable secret, nobody gets in.
# RUNOMICS_PRIVATE=1
# SESSION_SECRET=
# Google accounts that may view without being the owner, comma-separated - the
# other athlete's, say. Read on every request: removing one closes their session
# at the next deploy.
# RUNOMICS_VIEWERS=someone@gmail.com
#
# The Sync button in Settings (owner-only) dispatches sync.yml through the
# GitHub API on the server, so no phone or browser ever holds this token.
# A fine-grained PAT on this repository with Actions: Read and write - that
# is the only permission a workflow_dispatch needs.
# Without GITHUB_SYNC_TOKEN and GITHUB_SYNC_REPO the button answers 503 and
# says which one is missing; nothing else in the app depends on them.
# GITHUB_SYNC_TOKEN=a-fine-grained-github-pat-with-actions-read-and-write
# GITHUB_SYNC_REPO=your-username/RunOmics-Private
# Optional. Defaults below; set PROFILE so one athlete's deployment dispatches
# that athlete's sync rather than the whole matrix.
# The button's limits (one run at a time, 10 min between manual syncs, 12 a
# day: src/lib/syncLimits.ts) are read from this workflow's runs for PROFILE.
# The token's Actions: Read is what lists them.
# GITHUB_SYNC_WORKFLOW=sync.yml
# GITHUB_SYNC_REF=main
# GITHUB_SYNC_PROFILE=adam

# --- The private dataset ---
# Canonical local data checkout. The app, coaching CLI, and Python sync all honor
# this path. Keep it outside this code repository and outside public/.
# A typical layout has runomics-private/ and runomics-data-adam/ as siblings.
# RUNOMICS_DATA_DIR=../runomics-data-adam/data
#
# The private data repository. Without RUNOMICS_DATA_DIR, scripts/prepare-data.mjs
# fetches it into root data/, outside public/ so the dataset is never served as a
# static asset. Leave both unset for a portfolio/demo clone: a deterministic
# synthetic dataset is generated instead (npm install && npm run dev just works).
# Must be https:// (not git@/ssh://) - scripts/fetch_private_data.mjs and
# scripts/push_private_data.mjs authenticate over HTTPS via GIT_ASKPASS,
# reading the token only from this process's own environment, never as a
# URL/argument, so it never lands in `ps`, .git/config, or a build log.
# RUNOMICS_DATA_REPO_URL=https://github.com/your-username/runomics-data-adam
#
# A fine-grained GitHub PAT scoped to *only* that one repository.
# - Vercel (the build's fetch, and RUNOMICS_DATA_SOURCE=github): Contents: Read-only.
# - The sync.yml GitHub Environment (push_private_data.mjs) needs
#   Contents: Read and write instead - a second, separately-scoped PAT.
# Set an expiration and rotate it periodically; fine-grained PATs support both.
# RUNOMICS_DATA_REPO_TOKEN=a-fine-grained-github-pat-scoped-to-that-one-repo
#
# With github, a deployment also reads that repository at run time through
# GitHub's API, so a sync shows without a rebuild.
# RUNOMICS_DATA_SOURCE=github

# --- AI ---
# Informational/presentational RunOmics AI: Today insight, Week Purpose, Season,
# Analytics, run verdicts, PB celebration, shoe verdicts. Without it every card
# falls back to its rules-based copy. Keys at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-general-gemini-key
# Optional, for when Google retires a model (live list: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models):
# GEMINI_MODEL replaces the Flash pool (today, fresh verdicts, PB, shoes),
# GEMINI_BACKFILL_MODEL the Flash-Lite pool that backfills older run verdicts.
# GEMINI_MODEL=
# GEMINI_BACKFILL_MODEL=
# Only for `npm run coach ... --advisor gemini`; the coach itself runs through
# Claude Code with no key. A separate Google project on purpose - neither key ever
# falls back to the other, so the two free-tier quotas stay independent. Nothing
# deployed reads it, so it belongs in the coach's .env.<profile>.local only.
# GEMINI_COACH_API_KEY=your-coach-gemini-key
# Optional coaching-only model override for the manual preview command.
# GEMINI_COACH_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash
# Optional: Explore's route generator, which draws loops through the quartier
# to explore next. An OpenRouteService key from account.heigit.org - the free
# Standard plan allows 2000 directions a day and 40 a minute, shared by every
# deployment that uses the same key. Server-only: the generator calls ORS from
# the server (src/app/api/explore/route), and HeiGIT's terms forbid a key in a
# browser, so never give it a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name. Unset, the generator answers
# 503 and says so; the Districts layer and coverage work without it.
# ORS_API_KEY=your-openrouteservice-key
